From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] power: qcom_battmgr: refresh supplies after service startup

The Qualcomm battery manager registers its power-supply devices before the
PMIC GLINK protection-domain service is available.  This is required because
notifications can race the service-state callback, but it means that the
initial power-supply uevents can legitimately return -EAGAIN.  Proxmox's
early udev scan writes ``change`` to each power-supply uevent file and turns
that transient state into a visible error.

Ignore -EAGAIN while constructing a power-supply uevent, then emit one complete
change event after the battmgr notification request has succeeded.  The
normal property reads continue to return -EAGAIN until the firmware is ready;
no fake battery values are exposed.

---
 drivers/power/supply/power_supply_sysfs.c |  7 +++++--
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c       | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_sysfs.c b/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_sysfs.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_sysfs.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_sysfs.c
@@ -539,10 +539,13 @@
 	dev_attr = &pwr_attr->dev_attr;
 
 	ret = power_supply_format_property((struct device *)dev, true, dev_attr, prop_buf);
-	if (ret == -ENODEV || ret == -ENODATA || ret == -EINVAL) {
+	if (ret == -ENODEV || ret == -ENODATA || ret == -EINVAL || ret == -EAGAIN) {
 		/*
 		 * When a battery is absent, we expect -ENODEV. Don't abort;
-		 * send the uevent with at least the PRESENT=0 property
+		 * send the uevent with at least the PRESENT=0 property.  A
+		 * Qualcomm PMIC GLINK service can also be temporarily unavailable
+		 * while it is starting; the next power-supply change event carries
+		 * the complete set of properties.
 		 */
 		return 0;
 	}
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1596,6 +1596,22 @@
 	ret = qcom_battmgr_request(battmgr, &req, sizeof(req));
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(battmgr->dev, "failed to request power notifications\n");
+	else {
+		/*
+		 * The supplies are registered before the service comes up so that
+		 * early notifications cannot dereference NULL.  Refresh them after
+		 * notification delivery has been enabled, which also gives early
+		 * userspace a reliable initial battery/charger state.
+		 */
+		if (battmgr->bat_psy)
+			power_supply_changed(battmgr->bat_psy);
+		if (battmgr->ac_psy)
+			power_supply_changed(battmgr->ac_psy);
+		if (battmgr->usb_psy)
+			power_supply_changed(battmgr->usb_psy);
+		if (battmgr->wls_psy)
+			power_supply_changed(battmgr->wls_psy);
+	}
 }
 
 static void qcom_battmgr_pdr_notify(void *priv, int state)
-- 
2.50.1
